it if just as I snapped the picture, this FBI guy smells my boutonniere? You snapped a picture with

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:01.080
the FBI there?

01:02:01.440 --> 01:02:03.220
Sure, there were a lot of them there.

01:02:03.490 --> 01:02:05.910
But this one guy, the guy with the nose,

01:02:06.330 --> 01:02:07.840
he kept getting in my way.

01:02:09.830 --> 01:02:11.710
So this is where you live, huh?

01:02:11.910 --> 01:02:12.750
It's very nice.

01:02:13.270 --> 01:02:15.850
I was lucky to be able to rent a room from such nice people

01:02:15.850 --> 01:02:16.830
as the armsbees.

01:02:18.120 --> 01:02:21.440
You can come in, but be quiet. They're probably asleep.

01:02:23.850 --> 01:02:28.030
Gee, it sure is

01:02:28.030 --> 01:02:28.810
a nice place.

01:02:30.030 --> 01:02:32.870
I haven't been into a living room for a long time.

01:02:32.870 --> 01:02:34.960
Without dummies, I mean.

01:02:34.960 --> 01:02:38.320
It hasn't been much fun for you, has it?

01:02:38.320 --> 01:02:44.460
Oh, Audrey, I don't know what I would have done without you.

01:02:44.460 --> 01:02:46.840
You just go sit down and make yourself comfortable.

01:02:46.840 --> 01:02:51.280
I'll get us something cool to drink.

01:02:51.280 --> 01:02:54.610
You know, I want to apologize for losing all that money.

01:02:54.610 --> 01:02:59.050
I guess roulette wheels are radioactive proof.

01:02:59.050 --> 01:02:59.640
Hello?

01:03:00.090 --> 01:03:03.200
- Extension 238, please.

01:03:03.200 --> 01:03:05.010
- Hello?

01:03:05.010 --> 01:03:08.290
- Dr. Rodell, this is Audrey Nelson.

01:03:08.290 --> 01:03:10.240
- Oh, yes, Miss Nelson.

01:03:10.240 --> 01:03:11.520
- Did you know the Blix Waterbury

01:03:11.520 --> 01:03:13.200
escaped from the hospital?

01:03:13.200 --> 01:03:15.320
- Yes, I did.

01:03:15.320 --> 01:03:16.690
- My house now?

01:03:16.690 --> 01:03:18.920
- Yes, I know.

01:03:18.920 --> 01:03:21.910
- Well, aren't you going to send the FBI over?

01:03:21.910 --> 01:03:25.190
- Why, do you need a chaperone?

01:03:25.190 --> 01:03:27.280
- Is this Dr. Rodell?

01:03:27.280 --> 01:03:29.320
- Yes, Audrey, this is Dr. Rodell.

01:03:29.320 --> 01:03:30.000
There's nothing to be given.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:32.080
concerned about. I thought Blix deserved

01:03:32.080 --> 01:03:33.680
a little recreation. So

01:03:33.680 --> 01:03:36.180
enjoy yourselves. Oh, and Audrey,

01:03:36.360 --> 01:03:38.320
keep an eye on that Geiger

01:03:38.320 --> 01:03:55.740
counter. That's how you really feel about

01:03:55.740 --> 01:03:57.890
Stan? Of course. Stan and I

01:03:57.890 --> 01:04:00.000
are just friends. It'd be pretty

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:02.060
hard for a girl to get serious about Stan.

01:04:02.500 --> 01:04:03.950
Her main competition would be

01:04:03.950 --> 01:04:06.050
Stan. Gosh, I'll bet he got

01:04:06.050 --> 01:04:07.850
sore when you walked out on him in the casino.

01:04:08.110 --> 01:04:09.910
Oh, I didn't walk out on him. He said he'd be

01:04:09.910 --> 01:04:11.770
back in a half an hour, and I waited almost

01:04:11.770 --> 01:04:14.470
two hours. I can't imagine him

01:04:14.470 --> 01:04:16.690
standing you up. Nothing would be that

01:04:16.690 --> 01:04:18.710
important. Well, he's probably out making

01:04:18.710 --> 01:04:20.610
another deal to cash in on your name.

01:04:21.130 --> 01:04:22.690
Well, sure, Audrey, Stan makes all the deals

01:04:22.690 --> 01:04:24.710
for me, but don't forget, I get ten percent of everything.

01:04:25.230 --> 01:04:26.940
I still don't like the way he's

01:04:26.940 --> 01:04:29.280
exploiting you. Oh, look, let's...

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:31.040
Let's not talk about Stan.

01:04:31.390 --> 01:04:33.710
I only have a few hours left of freedom.

01:04:34.310 --> 01:04:35.910
Let's just concentrate on us.

01:04:39.020 --> 01:04:40.820
Your Geiger counter's ticking.

01:04:44.050 --> 01:04:49.100
Sometimes I wonder whether this thing is for me or against me.

01:04:50.430 --> 01:04:53.930
Awful hot in here, isn't it?

01:04:54.230 --> 01:04:55.300
I hadn't noticed.

01:04:57.270 --> 01:04:58.890
I know what it is.

01:04:58.950 --> 01:04:59.690
It's the lights.

01:04:59.870 --> 01:05:00.000
They...

01:05:00.480 --> 01:05:07.080
They make the room awful warm.

01:05:07.080 --> 01:05:12.920
Gosh, it's cooler already, don't you think?

01:05:12.920 --> 01:05:17.010
But we don't want it too cool in here now, do we?

01:05:17.010 --> 01:05:22.300
You know, I feel quite honored sitting next to the most important man in the world.

01:05:22.300 --> 01:05:25.980
I'll bet there are lots of girls who'd like to trade places with me right now.

01:05:25.980 --> 01:05:28.230
Audrey, I'm not interested in a lot of girls.

01:05:28.230 --> 01:05:30.000
I just want to concentrate on one.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:32.170
Funny.

01:05:32.170 --> 01:05:33.380
What?

01:05:33.380 --> 01:05:38.510
I always pictured my dream man as being tall, dark, and handsome.

01:05:38.510 --> 01:05:42.220
And then you come along.

01:05:42.220 --> 01:05:43.520
Short.

01:05:43.520 --> 01:05:45.080
Red-headed.

01:05:45.080 --> 01:05:46.190
Radio-act.

01:05:46.190 --> 01:05:49.730
Audrey.

01:06:27.100 --> 01:06:29.280
chaperone in the room with you all the time.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:39.290
ever been kissed like that before in my life. Honest. Please don't. There seems to be another

01:06:39.290 --> 01:06:48.360
light on in the room someplace. It's you. You're glowing. Gosh, I've had a relapse. Oh, what a

01:06:48.360 --> 01:07:00.000
wonderful relapse it's been. Maybe we'd better not see each other anymore. You'd better go now. Well, all right. Won't

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:01.670
Won't you give me one little kiss goodnight?

01:07:01.670 --> 01:07:03.590
If it's safe.

01:07:03.590 --> 01:07:09.360
I don't mean a 20,000-volt kiss, I mean just one of those little short-circuit kisses.

01:07:09.360 --> 01:07:12.000
Be careful.

01:07:12.000 --> 01:07:14.210
I won't.

01:07:14.210 --> 01:07:25.560
What a man.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:04.380
I just can't imagine a nice young man like Stan Cooper dealing with foreign agents.

01:08:04.380 --> 01:08:07.520
Well, we're convinced that Cooper doesn't know Reynolds as a spy.

01:08:07.520 --> 01:08:09.470
He's only trying to make a fast dollar.

01:08:09.470 --> 01:08:10.350
Are you gonna pick him up?

01:08:10.350 --> 01:08:11.350
Not yet.

01:08:11.350 --> 01:08:16.530
We've let him keep the boutonniere camera, but we've stymied any move he's made to photograph strategic installations.

01:08:16.530 --> 01:08:19.620
So far, he's only led us to Reynolds.

01:08:19.620 --> 01:08:23.260
But we're hoping he'll take us to someone higher up in the espionage ring.

01:08:23.260 --> 01:08:24.260
Mm-hmm.

01:08:24.260 --> 01:08:26.340
Jim, what do you think these foreign agents are after?

01:08:26.340 --> 01:08:28.450
Surely not the secret of the bomb.

01:08:28.450 --> 01:08:30.000
They already have that.

01:08:30.760 --> 01:08:32.880
They're after Waterbury himself.

01:08:32.880 --> 01:08:35.080
They think, like most of the people in the world,

01:08:35.080 --> 01:08:36.500
that his survival of the blast

01:08:36.500 --> 01:08:41.270
must be the clue to some new scientific discovery.

01:08:41.270 --> 01:08:43.800
We're close to the answer now.

01:08:43.800 --> 01:08:46.190
And when the final results are assembled,

01:08:46.190 --> 01:08:49.990
it'll come as quite a surprise to everyone.

01:08:49.990 --> 01:08:52.570
Come in.

01:08:52.570 --> 01:08:54.210
Oh, Blitz, come on in.

01:08:54.210 --> 01:08:55.050
How are you, sir?

01:08:55.050 --> 01:08:55.900
Hi, Doctor.

01:08:55.900 --> 01:08:58.460
Miss Nelson tells me you two are thinking of getting married.

01:08:58.460 --> 01:08:59.730
Am I invited to the wedding?

01:09:00.060 --> 01:09:02.840
Well, sir, if we do get married, we're going to elope.

01:09:03.120 --> 01:09:04.040
Nobody's going to see it.

01:09:04.450 --> 01:09:05.570
Don't be too sure.

01:09:06.140 --> 01:09:06.680
Goodbye, doctor.

01:09:07.040 --> 01:09:07.720
So long, Blix.

01:09:07.920 --> 01:09:08.400
Goodbye, sir.

01:09:08.970 --> 01:09:10.330
Doctor, they said you wanted to see me.

01:09:10.570 --> 01:09:12.790
Blix, I think it's time for another treatment.

01:09:13.190 --> 01:09:13.930
Another treatment?

01:09:14.130 --> 01:09:16.250
Oh, doctor, how many more treatments am I going to have to have?

01:09:16.310 --> 01:09:17.730
Oh, I don't think it'll be too many.

01:09:18.030 --> 01:09:18.650
We'll see today.

01:10:25.880 --> 01:10:27.050
Please, please, don't you?

01:10:27.050 --> 01:10:28.900
- Facts, doctor, you have...

01:10:28.900 --> 01:10:30.000
Doctor, do you...

01:10:30.120 --> 01:10:32.600
Do you have all of the facts there about the treatments, I mean?

01:10:32.640 --> 01:10:33.380
Oh, yes, yes, yes.

01:10:33.800 --> 01:10:36.680
Dr. Rodell said three weeks ago that it would be any day now.

01:10:37.080 --> 01:10:37.880
What's the answer?

01:10:38.400 --> 01:10:43.060
Oh, um, well, maybe we'd better wait till Dr. Rodell gets here.

01:10:43.200 --> 01:10:46.280
Oh, but, doctor, look, don't you know that I'm the fellow that this is happening to?

01:10:46.700 --> 01:10:48.500
Don't I at least have a right to know the answer?

01:10:49.280 --> 01:10:50.380
Very well.

01:11:04.350 --> 01:11:06.880
Doctor, what does this all mean?

01:11:06.880 --> 01:11:10.660
Oh, well, I see no harm in telling you what it means.

01:11:10.660 --> 01:11:14.650
Putting it simply, it means that our latest findings are completely negative.

01:11:14.650 --> 01:11:17.400
You're no longer radioactive.

01:11:17.400 --> 01:11:21.180
Not radioactive. You mean, you mean, Doctor, that it's all gone?

01:11:21.180 --> 01:11:24.250
You are of no further scientific interest to us.

01:11:24.250 --> 01:11:26.390
I'm no longer a secret weapon?

01:11:26.390 --> 01:11:29.280
No, you're of no importance to your government any longer, Waterbury.

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:34.610
past five months we've given you every conceivable test and the results add up

01:11:34.610 --> 01:11:46.530
to a scientific zero. Zero. It's going to be hard trying to be a normal guy again,

01:11:48.190 --> 01:11:52.660
not glowing in the dark anymore, hitting the jackpots on the slot machines or

01:11:52.660 --> 01:11:59.000
endorsing mother goose's peanut butter. I'm turning in my Geiger counter, doctor.

01:12:00.380 --> 01:12:02.800
I wonder if Audrey will marry me now when she knows about this.

01:12:04.210 --> 01:12:06.330
Well, I've got to get back to work.

01:12:06.660 --> 01:12:08.720
We are detonating another nuclear weapon this afternoon.

01:12:09.250 --> 01:12:12.750
If I don't see you again, Waterbury, good luck.

01:12:12.990 --> 01:12:13.610
Thank you, Doctor.

01:12:20.440 --> 01:12:23.840
Well, Blex, Dr. Pang born break the good news to you?

01:12:24.910 --> 01:12:25.650
Yes.

01:12:26.000 --> 01:12:26.660
Why so solemn?

01:12:27.030 --> 01:12:30.000
I thought you'd be happy to know you're a normal human being again.

01:12:32.650 --> 01:12:35.190
It's a funny thing, Doctor.

01:12:35.190 --> 01:12:39.070
When I was nobody, I used to dream of the day that I'd be somebody.

01:12:39.070 --> 01:12:43.310
When I became somebody, all it meant was just a lot of examinations and being cooped up

01:12:43.310 --> 01:12:45.060
in a room.

01:12:45.060 --> 01:12:48.580
And I'd have given anything to have been nobody again.

01:12:48.580 --> 01:12:53.850
Now that I'm nobody again, I don't know what I want.

01:12:53.850 --> 01:12:55.730
There are a great many people like that place.

01:12:55.730 --> 01:13:00.000
You know the old saying, there are only two types of people in the world, those who are

01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:01.500
because they haven't got what they want

01:13:01.500 --> 01:13:03.720
and those who are unhappy because they have.

01:13:05.580 --> 01:13:09.900
Well, I guess I'll leave.

01:13:10.300 --> 01:13:12.400
You don't want me hanging around here anymore.

01:13:12.640 --> 01:13:14.600
Lex, let's not put it that way.

01:13:14.980 --> 01:13:17.860
You're welcome to drop in and see me anytime you feel like it.

01:13:18.700 --> 01:13:21.360
You mean, doctor, I can just go?

01:13:21.670 --> 01:13:23.060
You're free to go anywhere you please.

01:13:24.670 --> 01:13:25.750
Without the FBI?

01:13:26.210 --> 01:13:28.200
The FBI isn't guarding you anymore.

01:13:30.830 --> 01:13:31.880
- That's a relief.

01:13:31.880 --> 01:13:35.220
- Funny, that's what they said.

01:13:35.220 --> 01:13:37.420
Oh, by the way, Blix, I know the newspaper man

01:13:37.420 --> 01:13:39.760
will be looking for you, so I'm holding up the announcement

01:13:39.760 --> 01:13:42.000
