01:13:42.000 --> 01:13:46.380
That's done so you can make your own plans.

01:13:46.380 --> 01:13:48.790
- I don't know what plans I'm gonna make, Doctor.

01:13:48.790 --> 01:13:52.020
- Oh, now, I'm sure Audrey will take care of that.

01:13:52.020 --> 01:13:52.920
Good luck, Blix.

01:13:52.920 --> 01:13:54.130
- Thanks, Doc.

01:13:54.130 --> 01:13:55.390
- Oh, one other thing.

01:13:55.390 --> 01:13:56.870
I have a personal favor to ask you.

01:13:56.870 --> 01:13:58.070
- Sure.

01:13:58.070 --> 01:14:00.000
- We're setting off a nuclear weapon this afternoon

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:01.480
at five o'clock sharp.

01:14:01.480 --> 01:14:03.090
- Another bomb.

01:14:03.090 --> 01:14:06.820
- Would you, for heaven's sake, stay out of the area?

01:14:06.820 --> 01:14:08.420
- I will.

01:14:08.420 --> 01:14:12.010
Say, doctor, perhaps you can tell me,

01:14:12.010 --> 01:14:17.290
how did I survive the atom bomb blast?

01:14:17.290 --> 01:14:19.390
- I only hope you can remember the prayers you said

01:14:19.390 --> 01:14:21.720
when the bomb went off,

01:14:21.720 --> 01:14:23.880
because five months of careful research

01:14:23.880 --> 01:14:27.010
have shown us that only a miracle could have saved you.

01:14:31.120 --> 01:14:38.640
- Goodbye, Doctor. - Goodbye, Blex.

01:14:38.640 --> 01:14:45.600
You don't like any of those either?

01:14:45.600 --> 01:14:48.640
I could have bought better ones on postcards at the drugstore.

01:14:48.640 --> 01:14:50.640
Well, I think it was that boutonniere camera.

01:14:50.640 --> 01:14:52.210
It's hard to focus.

01:14:52.210 --> 01:14:54.580
That's why I bought this imported camera.

01:14:54.580 --> 01:14:57.050
I think it'll give us the results we want.

01:14:57.050 --> 01:15:00.000
You see, it has a 1.9 lens and I'm...

01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:06.460
playing games. You're no help to us. You're through. Through? You're kidding. What about

01:15:06.460 --> 01:15:12.180
our contract to do Blix's life story? You can't be serious. No one could possibly be

01:15:12.180 --> 01:15:17.370
that stupid. I'll say I'm not that stupid. A contract's a contract. Blix and I have a

01:15:17.370 --> 01:15:21.350
million bucks coming to us and we're going to collect every cent of it. Now, don't play

01:15:21.350 --> 01:15:26.730
innocent with me, Cooper. You sold out. You know as well as I do. It wasn't for any book

01:15:26.730 --> 01:15:28.590
that you were taking pictures of atomic research?

01:15:28.850 --> 01:15:30.000
What do you mean it wasn't?

01:15:32.040 --> 01:15:39.960
wasn't? As if you didn't know. Ah, you've been playing me for a dupe. I've just been a dope being

01:15:39.960 --> 01:15:47.350
played for a dupe. Now it all starts to line up. You weren't calling me Conrad, you were calling

01:15:47.350 --> 01:15:54.510
me Comrade. And the way your face turned white when I mentioned the FBI. Life story, huh?

01:15:55.090 --> 01:16:00.000
All right, Cooper, you can stop now. You're almost as bad an actor as you are

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:05.280
a photographer clear up your conscience any way you want a simple fact is you're

01:16:05.280 --> 01:16:10.620
of no use to us anymore well I'm not huh but I've got one further service to

01:16:10.620 --> 01:16:19.100
perform comrade operator operator put down that phone that's enough of the

01:16:19.100 --> 01:16:24.710
boy scout stuff sit down you might be of a little use to a shit the organization

01:16:24.710 --> 01:16:29.000
wants blicks waterberry and we intend to use him to do our own research well

01:16:29.000 --> 01:16:30.000
you're not going to get him through any help

01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:33.000
Go ahead and shoot. I deserve a hole in the head for being so stupid.

01:16:33.000 --> 01:16:34.000
Now you are being stupid.

01:16:34.000 --> 01:16:37.000
I'm being stupid. You're being stupid.

01:16:37.000 --> 01:16:39.980
Do you think that you can get within a mile of Blix Waterbury?

01:16:39.980 --> 01:16:42.800
Why, they have him so closely guarded in Atomic City,

01:16:42.800 --> 01:16:45.720
even the FBI has to get permission to get in to see him.

01:16:45.720 --> 01:16:48.720
And you're gonna lay your hands on him. Don't make me laugh.

01:16:48.720 --> 01:16:53.300
See who it is. And no tricks.

01:17:00.440 --> 01:17:04.390
- Hi, Stan. - Ah, no thanks. No Girl Scout cookies today.

01:17:04.390 --> 01:17:06.610
They can be such pests. Let's ignore them.

01:17:06.610 --> 01:17:10.470
- What's the idea? - Close the door.

01:17:10.470 --> 01:17:13.990
- Yeah, sure. - So, what's going on here?

01:17:13.990 --> 01:17:17.190
We don't have any laundry to send out today. Now get out of here.

01:17:17.190 --> 01:17:22.950
This is a business conference, Blix. Hold it!

01:17:22.950 --> 01:17:27.360
Well, Mr. Waterbury, speaking of the devil and then you appear.

01:17:27.360 --> 01:17:30.000
We were just discussing how important you are.

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:31.860
Even the FBI couldn't get in to see you.

01:17:32.040 --> 01:17:33.640
Flix, you jerk. What did you do? Sneak out again?

01:17:33.640 --> 01:17:34.280
I didn't sneak out again.

01:17:34.280 --> 01:17:34.460
Quiet!

01:17:35.760 --> 01:17:36.620
Come on, let's get moving.

01:17:36.700 --> 01:17:38.520
Oh, wait a minute. What's this all about, Stanley?

01:17:38.780 --> 01:17:42.580
In case you don't know, Mr. Reynolds is a lousy spy.

01:17:42.780 --> 01:17:45.240
A spy? A spy? I don't believe it.

01:17:45.340 --> 01:17:46.540
Yeah, they goofed with me.

01:17:46.860 --> 01:17:49.000
Now they want to take you out of here and experiment with you.

01:17:49.180 --> 01:17:51.950
